--- begin ---
PRE-REGISTRATION: layer overlap as the compiler's default, every container it reaches, warm dispatch A/B.
Desktop 2 (DESKTOP-CBL5NUA), 2026-10-15. Written before any timed dispatch of these builds. Their only device runs so
far are exactness checks (results/aie/overlap_default_exact_desktop2_*: heads, 300 dispatches each, YOLOv8n and
YOLOv8s with --silu-sigmoid and pose; overlap_default_exact_ws_desktop2_*: whole workspace, 300 dispatches each,
those three plus SESR M7 and the ResNet50 head). No timing from those runs is read.

Change under test: ignite-compile's new default turns layer overlap on wherever a build allows it (no host layer and
none of ring, weight buffer, box fills, stream sharing, split layers, dense recipe; int8 design; every pattern on the
8-byte grain). --no-overlap-layers is the barrier build, byte-identical to the stream before the change (checked on
YOLOv8s against the shipped control).

Pairs (control = --no-overlap-layers, test = the default; same commit, same flags otherwise):
  yolov8n_silu  build/df_yolov8n_silu_{bar,def}.ignite  (--silu-sigmoid, what Ignition's docs build)
  yolov8s_silu  build/df_yolov8s_silu_{bar,def}.ignite  (--silu-sigmoid)
  yolov8n_pose  build/df_yolov8n_pose_{bar,def}.ignite
  sesr_m7       build/df_sesr_m7_{bar,def}.ignite
Not timed: the ResNet50 head (one layer, no boundary: both streams byte-identical) and the 640 classifier (a host
layer blocks overlap: both streams byte-identical).

Method: tools/bench_dispatch_ab.py with the four --pair, --rounds 4 --iters 300 (real and all-NOP copies, one
process per run, order reversed every second round), under research-lowlevel.sh --npu; void unless
timing_eligible true. Hashes below.

Prediction: sign only. Each pair's real delta (test - control) negative. Magnitude is not predicted: only YOLOv8s
(without the SiLU sigmoid) has a traced boundary decomposition. For orientation only, not a rule: YOLOv8s's
earlier gain was -1.22 ms; SESR M7 has 9 layers (8 boundaries) and may gain little.

Rules, per pair, on the 4-round means:
- KILL: real delta > +0.05 ms, or the test lower in fewer than 3 of 4 rounds.
- PASS: real delta < 0 with the test lower in 4 of 4 rounds.
- else MARGINAL.
The default lands as built only if no pair reads KILL. A KILL pair means the default must exclude that container
class (or the change does not land) - decided after, in the open.
Reported, not verdict-bearing: each NOP delta; compute exposure change (real - NOP).
Named alternatives: drift (controlled by interleaving, 4 rounds, and every pair in one sitting); a different
instruction count (none: each pair's streams are the same size).

A hang, an exactness failure or contention voids the sitting.
--- end ---

